WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.480
Here are the best high-end
products I tested in 2022.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.980
Let's start with face products.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.040
The Nars Light Reflecting
Advanced Skincare foundation

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.990
is so lightweight on the skin.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.060
The coverage is on the
light to medium side,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.890
but I definitely think you can build it up

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.270
without it getting cakey.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.520
It makes your skin look
really fresh and dewy

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.840
without looking oily.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.200
The Haus Labs foundation blends
into the skin seamlessly.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.841
The coverage is on the lighter side

00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:25.074
but still buildable.

00:00:25.074 --> 00:00:26.700
It has skincare ingredients in it,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.130
and it actually feels like skincare.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.100
It feels like you have
absolutely nothing on your face.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.191
All of my other products

00:00:33.191 --> 00:00:34.682
blend on top of this beautifully,

00:00:34.682 --> 00:00:37.080
so this foundation is
a 10 out of 10 for me.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.510
This is the Summer
Fridays sheer skin tint.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.580
It's supposed to be
lightweight, hydrating,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.470
and very natural on the skin.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.900
I definitely think it's
all of those things.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.430
The coverage is obviously sheer,

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.440
but it evened out my skin nicely.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.390
This is a great everyday skin tint.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.400
I'm not a pot-concealer kind of person,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.070
but I really love this
REM Sweetener concealer.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.500
This concealer looks
thicker than it feels.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.790
I was actually surprised

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.130
at how lightweight it felt
when I was blending it out.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.050
And the coverage with this is amazing.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.020
The Kosas Revealer concealer
is so easy to work with

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.610
and blends out so quickly.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.040
The coverage is a bit
lighter than medium to me,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.600
but it covers enough.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.910
I also love the Cloud Set setting powder.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.490
It smooths everything
out almost instantly,

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.130
and it just gives a
really soft, blurred look.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.010
The One/Size Beauty Cheek
Clapper 3D blush trio

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.503
has three different formulas,

00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:27.960
a flex cream, a full-impact
matte, and a hypersheen.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.370
These are really pigmented,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.190
and they just look beautiful
and smooth on the skin.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.338
There are just so many
different ways you can use it,

00:01:34.338 --> 00:01:36.720
and all the formulas
work together so nicely.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.400
The Made for Shade bronze and sculpt trio

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.660
is also very pigmented

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.390
and adds a nice bronzy warmth to the skin.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.040
This is the Merit bronze balm,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.680
and it's supposedly the
"easiest bronzer ever."

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.630
It's definitely one of
the easiest bronzers

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.890
I think I've ever used.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.320
It takes little to no
effort to blend this out,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.750
and it didn't break up the
product I already had on.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.090
The Haus Labs Bio-Blurring
loose setting powder

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.730
definitely does blur the
skin and sets your makeup

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.980
without making it look dry or cakey.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.750
It's so soft and finely milled,

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.946
and it's also talc-free, which is great.

00:02:05.946 --> 00:02:07.183
Moving on to eye products.

00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:09.717
This is the Danessa
Myricks Beauty Lightwork IV

00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:11.011
Transcendence palette.

00:02:11.011 --> 00:02:12.844
It has four different formulas:

00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:15.494
velvet chromes, which are
color-shifting powders;

00:02:15.494 --> 00:02:18.030
pressed chrome flakes,
which are flaky toppers;

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.795
glass metallics, which are
super-reflective powders;

00:02:20.795 --> 00:02:22.032
and aqua chromes, which are

00:02:22.032 --> 00:02:24.330
water-activated duo-chrome pigments.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.520
There is so much going on in this palette,

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.800
but all the formulas apply beautifully.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.710
It's extremely pricey, and I
did get some slight fallout,

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.418
but the quality is there, and I think

00:02:33.418 --> 00:02:35.640
it's so much more versatile than it looks.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.380
Plus it can be used on the face, too.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.320
This is the KVD Dazzle
long-wear eyeshadow stick.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.170
It's supposed to be a
one-and-done type of product,

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.340
so you don't need primer.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.260
You just swipe it on and blend.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.940
It really does glide on easily,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.700
and it has so much
glitter and shimmer in it.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.340
It's like a way to do glitter
without any of the mess.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.030
These are the Kaleidos Epiphany
Glow Melt-On eyeliners.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.129
They're all multi-chrome,

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:00.570
so they have these
really cool color shifts.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.120
These are so easy to apply,

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.111
and the formula is really smooth.

00:03:04.111 --> 00:03:07.920
This MAC MACStack mascara is
super volumizing, which I love.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.990
It gives your lashes an instant lift,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.120
and I have really straight lashes.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.920
I think it makes them look long and full

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.270
without looking clumpy.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.130
Next, let's talk about lip products.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.445
The Fenty Skin Plush Puddin'
intensive recovery lip mask

00:03:20.445 --> 00:03:23.640
feels so moisturizing
and plush on the lips.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.170
The formula is very thick,

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.390
but I personally love that in a lip mask.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.760
My lips were so much
more soft and hydrated

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.800
after using this mask consistently.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.250
I'm obsessed with the Summer
Fridays lip butter balms.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.210
The formula is on the
thicker side, but not sticky.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.780
They feel really moisturizing,

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.750
and I like how they give
an almost lip-gloss effect.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.000
They all give a pretty
subtle wash of color,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.560
and they have this nice vanilla scent

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.970
that's not overpowering.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.250
The Item Beauty Lip Quip
moisturizing lip oil

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.800
smells amazing, kind of peachy.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.900
The color is actually
a little more pigmented

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.460
than I was expecting for a lip oil,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.080
but I think it's so pretty.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.277
It feels super nourishing,

00:03:59.277 --> 00:04:01.410
and it just makes your lips look so juicy.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.450
This is the Hourglass Cosmetics Phantom

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.950
volumizing glossy balm.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.350
It's supposed to be a
lip balm, lip plumper,

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.360
and a lip gloss all in one product.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.520
They have this really nice cooling effect,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.950
and they do feel like a
super-moisturizing lip balm

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.170
but have this high-shine
finish, like a gloss.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.060
It didn't do much for
me in terms of plumping,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.520
but I do love how these
look and feel on the lips.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.215
The Rare Beauty Kind Words
matte lipsticks and lip liners

00:04:23.215 --> 00:04:25.650
are the most comfortable
matte lip products.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.450
The lip liner is super smooth.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.283
Even though it's matte,

00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:30.391
it doesn't drag or pull on the lips.

00:04:30.391 --> 00:04:32.370
Plus it's a twist-up, which I love.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.620
The lipstick is so creamy and pigmented.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.600
You could probably put
this on in one swipe.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.700
This is the Nars Powermatte lipstick.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.980
It has really amazing color payoff.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.600
The texture is so unique.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.570
It's this soft, powdery,
comfortable kind of matte

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.730
that actually feels
really nice on the lips,

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.960
and it's transfer-proof.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.430
I highly recommend this one.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.890
This is the Fenty Beauty Icon semi-matte

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.180
refillable lipstick.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.180
So the case and the actual
lipstick are sold separately,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.040
and then you assemble them together.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.040
The pigment is incredible
and totally full coverage.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.010
It's just a very creamy
formula that feels so smooth

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.630
and hydrating on the lips.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.760
The Haus Labs Atomic Shake lip lacquer

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.550
is one of those transfer-proof
glossy lipsticks,

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.310
so you shake the product
well and then apply it.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.410
The pigment in this really shocked me.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.170
It was so vibrant, it almost looked neon.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.570
I didn't need more than one
layer for full coverage,

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.403
and it was so glossy.

